### The same calls as the demo scripts, one at a time.
### Works in Visual Studio, Rider and the VS Code REST Client.
### Start the service first: dotnet run --project src/GameOfLife.Api --launch-profile http

@base = http://localhost:8080

### Upload a blinker (3x3, horizontal phase). Returns 201 + Location.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/boards
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "width": 3,
  "height": 3,
  "cells": [
    [false, false, false],
    [true,  true,  true ],
    [false, false, false]
  ]
}

### Paste the id from the upload's Location header here.
@id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Board metadata and generation 0.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}

### One generation forward. Call it twice -- the answer does not change.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}/next

### Ten generations away. A blinker at an even index matches generation 0.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}/generations/10

### Final state. A blinker reports CYCLE with period 2.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}/final

### Final state with an explicit limit.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}/final?maxGenerations=50

### Final state that gives up. A blinker needs two steps to see its cycle, so a limit of 1 is 422.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}/final?maxGenerations=1

### 400: maxGenerations must be at least 1.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/{{id}}/final?maxGenerations=0

### 404: no board with this id.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/boards/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
